The endpoint that streams chat answers is defined in **`backend/main.py`** as a POST route named `/chat`.  
It is registered with the FastAPI `app` object and returns a `StreamingResponse` that feeds the generator from `agent.stream_answer`.

```py
@app.post("/chat")
def chat(body: ChatRequest):
    if body.repo_url not in _indexed_repos:
        raise HTTPException(
            status_code=404,
            detail=f"Repository not indexed. POST /index first: {body.repo_url}",
        )

    indexer = _indexed_repos[body.repo_url]["indexer"]

    return StreamingResponse(
        agent.stream_answer(indexer, body.question, body.history),
        media_type="text/event-stream",
        headers={"Cache-Control": "no-cache", "X-Accel-Buffering": "no"},
    )
```

This is the HTTP endpoint that answers chat questions. [lines 151‑178]
